From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:29:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] build: use tsrs for application checks and SDK
 declarations

Ship pinned tsrs with the CLI and use it for every configured application
check. Resolve its launcher relative to the installed SDK, including bundled
CommonJS and nested package-manager layouts. Remove compiler selection and
the obsolete project-local TypeScript version probe.

Force no emission for application checks, preserve watched-file observation
and concurrent-edit retries, and await diagnostic pipe closure. Accept an
empty project only when its no-inputs diagnostic is the sole reported error.
The existing enable, try and disable modes remain.

Use tsrs for SDK source checking and declaration emission. Generate public
and internal declarations once each, then copy the identical declarations
to their ESM and CommonJS package layouts. Keep package markers, declaration
maps and internal-API removal intact; esbuild still emits runtime JavaScript.
Describe ordinary buffer ownership without adding upload copies or requiring
generic typed-array syntax in public declarations.

Older tsc-based clients remain backend-compatible because checking does not
change deployment requests or emitted application JavaScript.

Keep machine-readable diagnostics unformatted, decode subprocess UTF-8 across
pipe chunks, and check explicit projects without bundling their application.
